  "details": "Let's be honest, VRChat is not safe for streamers and people who use personalized avatars. Private avatars being stolen and exploited way too many times. Players who want to use personalized avatars are endangered in game, that emphasizes social experience. \nSimple solution for that: allow players to decide who can see their avatar, preventing other people from accessing avatar data on API level. This should be controlled in many ways: ranking system, friend list, custom whitelist, user id. With new fallback system this feature gives new possibilities and much more freedom and safety to everyone. As the bonus it puts responsibility for own avatar data on user side. \nGive us a way to protect ourselves!",
